    "resource": "aws_default_route_table.default",
    "issue": "Default route table may remain with inherited default routes",
    "risk": "If `var.default_route_table_no_routes` is false or the resource is not created, the default route table may retain routes that allow unintended connectivity, including internet access when associated with an internet gateway.",
    "remediation": "Set `var.default_route_table_no_routes = true` so `aws_default_route_table.default` is created and managed. Ensure the resource contains no `route` blocks unless explicitly required and reviewed."
  },
  {
    "resource": "aws_default_network_acl.default",
    "issue": "Default network ACL may remain with permissive allow-all rules",
    "risk": "If `var.default_network_acl_deny_all` is false or the resource is not created, the default network ACL can retain AWS default allow-all ingress and egress rules, weakening subnet-level traffic filtering.",
    "remediation": "Set `var.default_network_acl_deny_all = true` so `aws_default_network_acl.default` is created and managed. Explicitly configure restrictive `ingress` and `egress` rule blocks instead of relying on the AWS defaults."
  },
  {
    "resource": "aws_internet_gateway.default",
    "issue": "Internet gateway can expose the VPC to direct internet routing",
    "risk": "When `var.internet_gateway_enabled` is true, public routing can be established for attached subnets, increasing the attack surface and the chance of unintended internet exposure.",
    "remediation": "Set `var.internet_gateway_enabled = false` unless internet access is strictly required. If it is required, ensure only intended public subnets have route table entries to `aws_internet_gateway.default` and protect workloads with restrictive security groups and NACLs."
  }
